				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238168" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1535832540 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Sep 2018 20:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3949601">
									

<p>Okay, so this was a really fun project that actually didn't take too long to finalize because we hit the ground running with the ideas. <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/alces-alces" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4057128); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4057128&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1535836126" alt="Alces_alces" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4057128)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/alces-alces" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4057128); return false;">Alces_alces</a></span> (whose carabiner SCP I really like) originally reached out to me asking for feedback on the draft, and I reviewed it while pretty tired and crabby (sorry, Alces) but then later came back to read it again and found that I really liked the concept and the overall tone. We talked about a few polish-up tweaks and story elements, edits were made, we got feedback from lots of people (thank you all so, so much!) and now here we are.</p>
<p>When reading the original draft, I was getting vibes of mythological golems created out of simple materials and given life (using a piece of paper or through a word of power written on its forehead) to serve masters. And it got me thinking, what happens to a golem whose master is gone? What happens to a golem who doesn't want to perform its former tasks? What does a golem do with its freedom?</p>
<p>Also I had the mental image of samurai, who would be bloodthirsty on the battlefield, but engage in artistic pursuits like flower arrangement to purify the heart and mind.</p>
<p>To those reading, thanks for your time, and I hope you enjoy the piece!</p>
<p>ETA: also, Alces made the twine man in the picture! How cool is that?</p>

